     xmlns:OntologiaLOPDP="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#"
     xmlns:ontopriv-gdpr-alignment="http://www.semanticweb.org/profiles/ontopriv-gdpr-alignment#"
     xmlns:ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales="http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://elian18.github.io/ontology-integration-transformer/">
        <terms:abstract xml:lang="es">Base de conocimiento legal construida a partir de OntoPriv y de la Ley Orgánica de Protección de Datos Personales del Ecuador (LOPDP), alineada con el Data Privacy Vocabulary (DPV) y enlazada con el GDPR por medio de GDPRtEXT.</terms:abstract>
        <terms:abstract xml:lang="en">Legal knowledge base built from OntoPriv and Ecuador&apos;s Organic Law on Personal Data Protection (LOPDP), aligned with the Data Privacy Vocabulary (DPV) and linked to the GDPR through GDPRtEXT.</terms:abstract>
        <terms:bibliographicCitation>E. A. Gavilanes Miranda, «Base de conocimiento legal de privacidad: OntoPriv-LOPDP alineada con el DPV y el GDPR», versión 1.1.0, Escuela Politécnica Nacional, 2026.</terms:bibliographicCitation>
        <terms:creator rdf:nodeID="genid1"/>
        <terms:description xml:lang="en">Brings together in one document the four modules of the base: the reusable core (OntoPriv-Core), the Ecuador profile (LOPDP), the alignment with the DPV approved by human review and the bridge with the GDPR (GDPRtEXT). Based on OntoPriv, by G. Suntaxi, K. Ojeda and F. Rodríguez (CLEI 2024), and on its DPV-based version, by G. Suntaxi, K. Ojeda, F. Rodríguez, P. del Hierro, J. Miño and D. A. Flores (2025). The sentence of each concept with its correspondences is written only for this documentation; the modules of the repository do not have it. Some terms of OntoPriv have two types at once, for example class and property (OWL Full): their entry does not show the sentence, but the table below does.

### Correspondences of the base

| Concept | DPV | GDPR | Articles of the LOPDP |
|---|---|---|---|
